[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-161445"] :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<1-x}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/5151df3c5b84ffaca9aa16b401cd9364fea10a240d39c9c28d815b36e417b16d.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-161624/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "bc6718f6-4976-57b6-b370-f79e3466cb78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161624/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "0c1363c9-8a00-510f-a8af-9a584d6f4f2a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161624/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "3eda1123-fb27-58ee-b348-baf8461c20c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161624/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "9be9472c-4118-5314-9f01-1e88064b98a5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161624/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "f3aed6ca-2b03-5dde-a451-aa62b960f5b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161624/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ad2ca6b-d482-5608-9f02-2e57e713f54b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161624/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-161624/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-161624/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-161624/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-161624/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-161624/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161624" :question/id #uuid "318629c1-2457-50a8-91b8-67b30dc4061b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161624" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/8414de2e05da43c03fae3c8b1ff2102401e990188e9fd4ee59a24308ec34b086.png)\n\n \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. As we have seen, $∂A$ consists of two concentric circles: the outer one is in $A,$ while the inner one is not.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ contains some of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161624/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161624"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161718/selection/915fe4cb8c55e3c7dcc9ec2ff1f82206691ae76e0e2c2c4c63b0329b65cedba1" :answer/id #uuid "6f724aae-8b8f-5b82-bac0-67f022cb60ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x\\le y\\le x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161718/selection/cf79a37461d9f1799e113418cf10a8fc23e22072ab51cf1f0b84e973d7e3b90e" :answer/id #uuid "1befd6ec-4f43-5a5a-90de-6227f6e4bdee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x\\le y<x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161718/selection/06cb469c1f1b43d5e4ec26129aef41fbca4f7518024ee8e4ee70b5314a141c45" :answer/id #uuid "07cb221d-6254-54c9-b93b-66f9c21ca222" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<y\\le x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161718/selection/ea1d844bbf18ca365b9c89547442958a79ca8a680be023a02a940f189bfb3a43" :answer/id #uuid "1f006973-3acf-581b-842a-d7f56833fef0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<y<x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161718/selection/d580513db1f50c0e9f075a59068eaeb2bde35b3d522d8a6ad002df3ed2844740" :answer/id #uuid "fd49e677-9cf8-59d2-abc2-ae8a5ae11b85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x<y<x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161718/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "85c065e2-d4a7-5f6e-aa29-d60489c19beb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161718/selection/d580513db1f50c0e9f075a59068eaeb2bde35b3d522d8a6ad002df3ed2844740" :answer-field/choices ["q-161718/selection/915fe4cb8c55e3c7dcc9ec2ff1f82206691ae76e0e2c2c4c63b0329b65cedba1" "q-161718/selection/cf79a37461d9f1799e113418cf10a8fc23e22072ab51cf1f0b84e973d7e3b90e" "q-161718/selection/06cb469c1f1b43d5e4ec26129aef41fbca4f7518024ee8e4ee70b5314a141c45" "q-161718/selection/ea1d844bbf18ca365b9c89547442958a79ca8a680be023a02a940f189bfb3a43" "q-161718/selection/d580513db1f50c0e9f075a59068eaeb2bde35b3d522d8a6ad002df3ed2844740"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161718" :question/id #uuid "9cae3814-ea99-54e9-86e7-c0bc019bdf37" :question/math-academy-id "q-161718" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/af1e6e7b384732a527fc77e9729c6e02aaa288d4076c030c9fae58742cb10f74.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/0a0b92621d83d6395926a75b5cae34f479a8b9e64dfe82711094c3724b3b3220.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/3ddef68bf4b4284c1b68896920fddb8d7fb0e70eba15dee103cdbc0134a9ed20.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,-x<y<x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161718/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161718"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161730/selection/17508a139062a9b846fa19685eb8a9780b23e2d8ee825f49e6bbe17221c114b5" :answer/id #uuid "0da8d515-7cc0-506d-abb2-6c7a21926771" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<y<2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161730/selection/dbaf85835946aefb97564ba0d1ea287b684a4c8821f4256502e349376df74d28" :answer/id #uuid "fb486883-b547-52d1-b198-5104c36a9bbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161730/selection/17fbc9b20d7e4eea412c13d7824720e52854f930779d36ddd065ff7ffba70ec9" :answer/id #uuid "4c2617a0-7b87-51fe-9e98-a57527022afa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\le y\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161730/selection/73ec1de0e5f7b20f7a58afa48ad0988678999337d226efd9e7951949e484fd24" :answer/id #uuid "2f2db1fd-ef9f-52cf-8fd2-c24e6c710a89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0\\le y\\le 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161730/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" :answer/id #uuid "8761eec8-3cc6-5877-b192-11245ef0e21c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161730/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9210ab2-eeb9-5f7b-b9eb-272b79a0921a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161730/selection/17508a139062a9b846fa19685eb8a9780b23e2d8ee825f49e6bbe17221c114b5" :answer-field/choices ["q-161730/selection/17508a139062a9b846fa19685eb8a9780b23e2d8ee825f49e6bbe17221c114b5" "q-161730/selection/dbaf85835946aefb97564ba0d1ea287b684a4c8821f4256502e349376df74d28" "q-161730/selection/17fbc9b20d7e4eea412c13d7824720e52854f930779d36ddd065ff7ffba70ec9" "q-161730/selection/73ec1de0e5f7b20f7a58afa48ad0988678999337d226efd9e7951949e484fd24" "q-161730/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161730" :question/id #uuid "02d084df-878c-5b52-8acb-7b7ee4dbdd09" :question/math-academy-id "q-161730" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/aa335a55f5b4496cdaccca5d35e286a168598761188bc520c81397ef136f927d.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/fba9ba3e52ed19eb0bb2286ae59c49bb9dc648134d9eab3c4e2d13862963f736.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/2f3cd30dbaa4f84c43f2a7f1197aa904e3d43b1212241ae26736b2a0087f6170.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<y<2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161730/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161730"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161731/selection/90cba21841919a576751718b03eb9c72a0a5b7934542dd9f2f1e14515ca246a6" :answer/id #uuid "9db3281b-b340-5f08-8e81-e177d5ceb825" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161731/selection/05dc4c115c1163e1b799c636e274c9de72100fd5a5b1b2515ac780135031c4c0" :answer/id #uuid "200e92b1-e2b3-5589-979a-cfdf33ec04bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<y<\\frac{2}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161731/selection/483f87082abf6e24451d1d37b8b1017accd1998c536507d68aa76959d57ec5ab" :answer/id #uuid "ff23d5f1-240e-57b7-b037-2856b86c8238" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0\\le y\\le \\frac{2}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161731/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" :answer/id #uuid "12f3fa0f-8c5d-50ca-a4ae-20b159472d61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161731/selection/20bbea9cb70fd2c9aa3a462eb45adc30e35fd231e1826c487d0492a58b0d2776" :answer/id #uuid "b7e4940b-f327-53ce-8c5d-416061ae5ba8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}x<y<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161731/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed9b2810-dcbe-5c0f-b69b-0d58bc3542a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161731/selection/05dc4c115c1163e1b799c636e274c9de72100fd5a5b1b2515ac780135031c4c0" :answer-field/choices ["q-161731/selection/90cba21841919a576751718b03eb9c72a0a5b7934542dd9f2f1e14515ca246a6" "q-161731/selection/05dc4c115c1163e1b799c636e274c9de72100fd5a5b1b2515ac780135031c4c0" "q-161731/selection/483f87082abf6e24451d1d37b8b1017accd1998c536507d68aa76959d57ec5ab" "q-161731/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" "q-161731/selection/20bbea9cb70fd2c9aa3a462eb45adc30e35fd231e1826c487d0492a58b0d2776"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161731" :question/id #uuid "7db58d1f-c945-5982-b978-7bc405280419" :question/math-academy-id "q-161731" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/8d7ceac8c936a745ae79f71844a6d1a74175b1b97a2a497588d34c9ff988cdf9.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<3,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/c0e6ef400b15c54264a400af99bef64c3bb5aeb7ceadbdd599375c0f1e0d3642.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/8c5bbdfca6736194791f834ab4aadb03a30e3f116e89ffd5a7ea3e0104708ae4.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<3,\\,0<y<\\frac{2}{3}x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161731/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1d